8. ESCROW AND FINANCIAL SAFETY
==================================================

Audit the existing escrow-related code before extending it.

Preserve existing working escrow logic and explain any required changes.

Design financial operations so that they can be reconciled and audited.

Where legally and technically supported, account for:

- Payment initiation.
- Payment confirmation.
- Funds-held status.
- Order fulfillment.
- Buyer confirmation or approved dispute resolution.
- Refunds.
- Vendor settlement.
- Transaction history.
- Administrative review.
- Failed and reversed transactions.

IMPORTANT:

Do not describe a database status field as real escrow custody.

Do not claim that Rwandamket securely holds customer funds unless the
actual payment and custody arrangements support that claim.

Use a properly authorized payment provider and verify the applicable
financial and regulatory requirements before enabling any custody,
escrow, or payout functionality.

Never mark an order as paid merely because the browser redirects to a
success page.

Verify payment status using authenticated server-to-server callbacks,
provider verification APIs, or the provider's documented secure mechanism.

Verify callback signatures and prevent replay attacks where supported.

Use idempotency controls to prevent duplicate charges, refunds, and payouts.

Do not store card numbers, security codes, payment passwords, or mobile
money PINs.

Never invent payment provider credentials, API responses, or successful
transactions.

If payment credentials or regulatory approvals are missing, implement
safe integration boundaries and clearly document what remains blocked.

